 "notes": "Approximate digitization; not supplied or endorsed by Kodak Alaris / Eastman Kodak Company. Sensitometry x = (log H - Log H Ref) / log10(2), Log H Ref -0.84 lux-seconds read from the characteristic-curve chart; density is Status M including base, made monotone by running maximum. Spectral sensitivity kept only where the curve is drawn on the chart; wavelengths where a curve is not drawn are omitted, so a channel's wavelength list can be non-contiguous. Individual dye curves not published; dye_density holds only the published midscale neutral and minimum density curves. E-2519 covers SUPRA 100, 400 and 800; only the SUPRA 100 page (page 7) and the SUPRA 100 row of the Print Grain Index table (page 6) are used. Characteristic curves: Exposure Daylight, Densitometry Status M, Log H Ref -0.84 (no process line printed on the chart; the datasheet specifies Process C-41); axes calibrated from the drawn tick marks (log H -3.0 and 1.0, density 1.0 and 3.0), which agree with the frame (log H -4.0..2.0, density 0.0..4.0). Spectral sensitivity: Effective exposure 1/25 s, Status M, density 0.2 above D-min; axes calibrated from the drawn grid lines (400 and 700 nm, log sensitivity 0.0 and 3.0); the blue and green curves are two subpaths of one PDF path and are separated by subpath. Spectral dye density: typical densities for D-min and a midscale neutral subject; the midscale neutral curve leaves the top of the frame (2.5) near 400 nm and is kept as drawn (about 2.54 at 400 nm). Print Grain Index table as published (page 6): only 24 x 36 mm (135) negatives, print sizes in inches; no RMS granularity and no MTF chart are published, so the loader's granularity fallback applies.",
